# Olympus — post-gate backlog, waved by DEFECT CLASS — 2026-08-12
#
# GOAL: work the open backlog in the order that finds the most defects per
# hour, rather than in priority order.
#
# WHY CLASS BEATS PRIORITY — measured on 2026-08-11/12, not assumed.
#   The fabricated-data class had SEVEN instances. Exactly ONE was filed by
#   a human. Every other was found by FOLLOWING a fix:
#     #2537 (savings from the day of the month) -> its sweep found #2540
#     #2521 (match % = provider ordering) -> #2541 -> #2548
#     #2540's sweep found #2551 (the PRD itself instructs the fabrication)
#   Same shape in unfalsifiable-guard: 3 instances, 1 filed, 2 downstream.
#   Priority ordering cannot see that. It interleaves unrelated work and
#   loses the pattern between PRs.
#
# THE HEADLINE NUMBER
#   ⚠ PROVISIONAL - DO NOT PLAN HEADCOUNT OR TIMELINES AGAINST 155/112.
#   The non-defect classes below sum to 69 plus 2 unclassified, which implies
#   ~196 defects, not 155. One of the two numbers is wrong and the recount has
#   not been done. The SHAPE of the argument survives either way (class beats
#   priority; the non-defects belong off the wave track). The number does not.
#
#   267 open issues. 155 are defects. The other 112 are features (28),
#   chores (22), compliance documents (14), ops gates (5) and similar.
#   Those must NOT be waved by defect class - they need their own track.
#   Mixing them in is why the backlog reads as unmanageable.
#
#   Only 16 issues (~6%) are closeable. The speed-filed cohort is NOT full
#   of duplicates: the reviewers cited each other and split deliberately by
#   mechanism. The backlog is large because the defects are real.
#
# THE RE-FRAME THAT CHANGES THE ORDER
#   The fabrication class keeps regenerating after two sweeps because the
#   sweeps were pointed at the CODE and the source is the PRD.
#   #2551 is not one bad paragraph, it is a policy across six spec pages.
#   The PRD contradicts itself about it:
#     docs/prd/pages/booked-v2.md:316          FORBIDS the Tokyo fixture
#     docs/prd/pages/09-bookings-detail.md:1120 MANDATES it
#   An implementer reading either page is following the PRD. That single
#   contradiction has already produced THREE implementations in the code.
#
#   Two things make it urgent rather than tidy:
#     1. The premise it was ratified under expires this week.
#        20-stories.md:7 records it verbatim: "sandbox/demo posture - no
#        real users". False the moment the F&F cohort is invited.
#     2. scripts/voice-lint.sh globs only *.go *.ts *.tsx. It CANNOT read
#        a .md file. The document defining every user-facing string in the
#        product is structurally unlintable. That is the mechanism that let
#        all of this accumulate.
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WAVE ORDER, and why each earns its slot
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THIS IS A PRIORITY OF YIELD, NOT A SERIAL SCHEDULE. What actually runs is
# the highest-value work available under non-conflicting scopes, with class
# order as the default when value and scope allow. Round 3 dispatched #2555,
# #2556 and #2557 - all Wave 4 - ahead of Waves 2 and 3, because they are
# money and fundraising surfaces. That was correct. Do not read the numbering
# as a dispatch order.
