# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEFINITION OF DONE — an issue is not done when its PR merges
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Every issue walks the full chain. `scripts/land.sh <PR#>` automates the
# mechanical parts; the judgement parts are listed at the end of its output
# and stay manual on purpose.
#
#   1. CRITIC     no PR merges without one. 5 of 5 on 2026-08-12, and every
#                 one found something wrong with the producer's CLAIMS rather
#                 than its code.
#   2. MERGE ORDER - THE HARD GATE THAT IS NOT AUTOMATED, AND IS NOT OPTIONAL.
#                 Before landing two PRs that can COUPLE - same subsystem OR
#                 shared test surface - merge them LOCALLY and run the suite.
#                 mergeStateStatus CLEAN IS NOT SAFETY. #2568 and #2561 shared
#                 NO FILE, both reported CLEAN, and the second to land would
#                 have reddened main with no warning from git. Nothing but
#                 running the combined tree finds this. land.sh cannot do it
#                 for you and says so.
#   3. CI GREEN   poll `.status == "completed"`. `.conclusion // "RUNNING"`
#                 does NOT catch an empty string and exits immediately.
#   4. MERGE      then RE-CHECK the issue state. A squash can drop the
#                 `Closes #N` keywords and the issue silently stays open.
#                 #2374 and #2418 both did this.
#   5. MAIN GREEN a red main silently deadlocks the entire merge queue -
#                 every open PR inherits UNSTABLE and "Ready: 0" reads as
#                 quiet rather than as a jam.
#   6. DEPLOY     only if the diff touches shippable code. A test-only change
#                 has nothing to deploy and must not be reported as deployed.
#   7. PROD       ask the service which commit it is running. A green deploy
#                 run is not a deploy; a 9-second success is a gate skip.
#                 Compare against the newest apps/api commit, NOT origin/main:
#                 the API only deploys on apps/api/**, so lagging main after a
#                 web-only merge is healthy.
#   8. VERIFY THE CLAIM - AND SPLIT THE TWO KINDS. Never report them as one.
#                 (a) EXTERNALLY VERIFIED: probed on the live service. #2574
#                     (parse veto on prod), #2486 (sweeper running, from Cloud
#                     Logging, control query first).
#                 (b) NO PUBLIC PROBE EXISTS: internal behaviour with no
#                     externally observable surface. #2568 (booking-store
#                     conformance), #2413 (mock locality rung - mock_active is
#                     false in prod so the path is unreachable there).
#                 (b) is a legitimate outcome, but it must be NAMED as such.
#                 It is not a second kind of green.
#                 Not that the page loads. Assert the specific thing
#                 the PR said it fixed. RUN THE CONTROL FIRST: on 2026-08-12 a
#                 probe of 904KB of prod bundle returned 0 for the new string
#                 AND 0 for `Confirm & Pay`, so the corpus could not see the
#                 surface and every 0 was meaningless.
#   9. SAY WHAT WAS NOT VERIFIED   that beats a green probe implying coverage
#                 it does not have.
#  10. CLOSE      with a receipt naming the merge SHA and the evidence.
#                 status:qa is ONLY for something a human must look at.
#
# THE FOUR WAYS A FAIL-FIRST PROOF LIED THIS WEEK — in every brief until they
# live in a skill file:
#   a) a perl -0pi syntax error left the source pristine and the suite passed
#   b) a mutation landed in the error branch and failed to COMPILE; a naive
#      runner reports that as RED
#   c) git clean -fd deleted worktree node_modules symlinks, so six "reds"
#      were module-resolution errors. Turbopack also rejects a node_modules
#      SYMLINK in a worktree - use a hardlink tree (cp -al) or --webpack.
#   d) a nil-deref panic killed the test binary early: two failures at 2.7s
#      against a 14.3s baseline, reading as the OPPOSITE conclusion.
#      RECORD THE BASELINE DURATION BEFORE MUTATING.
#
# And one that bit the orchestrator, not an agent:
#   e) the Go module root is apps/api. `go test` from the repo root gives
#      `[setup failed]`, which reads exactly like a real break.

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PROD VERIFICATION PLAN — written BEFORE the PR lands, not after
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Deciding how to prove something after it merges is how a green badge gets
# accepted as evidence. Each in-flight PR gets its check defined up front,
# including an honest "not externally observable" where that is the truth.
#
# ── ROUND 1, LANDED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# #2566 (#2374 #2418)  test-only. NOTHING TO VERIFY ON PROD, and it must not
#     be reported as deployed. Evidence is CI: 316 files / 4489 tests, plus
#     the counterfactual (bare string assertion + bug = 33 passed, 0 failed).
#
# #2564 (#2559)  test-only, same. Evidence is the E2E critical job executing
#     (not skipped) and the three a11y tests passing by name.
#
# #2561 (#2558)  test-only. Evidence is the nine formerly-skipped tests now
#     running, each red under a reviewer-applied mutation.
#
# #2568 (#2318 #1108)  PRODUCTION CODE. Live on prod as 257ad922, confirmed by
#     asking the service its version. The behaviour itself (uuid rejection at
#     the store, orphan predicate parity) is INTERNAL and has no public
#     endpoint - SAY SO rather than inventing a probe. Strongest available
#     evidence is CI's Postgres Integration job running the conformance suite
#     against a real container, plus the reviewer breaking the POSTGRES store
#     and watching the suite redden.
#
# ── ROUND 2, IN FLIGHT — checks defined now ────────────────────────────────
#
# PR #2570 (#2477 #2486) orphan detector runner + funnel
#     PROD CHECK: after deploy, query Cloud Logging for the detector actually
#     firing on a schedule. This is the one issue whose whole point is
#     reachability, so "the code is live" is NOT the check - "it ran" is.
#     CAUTION: nothing in infra/monitoring is APPLIED in GCP (verified
#     2026-08-11, policies/metrics/channels all empty). A merged alert
#     definition pages NOBODY until someone applies the file. If the PR
#     implies otherwise, send it back.
#
# PR #2571 (#2401 #2413) fixture contract + missing locality codes
#     PROD CHECK: the locality table is production code. Probe the live API
#     with KEF, IDR and GOA and assert a NON-EMPTY origin. Run a control
#     first with a code known to resolve - if the control fails, the probe
#     cannot see the surface and every result is meaningless.
#     The fixture half is test-only: nothing to verify, say so.
#
# PR #2574 (#2342 #2335) hotel-path guards
#     PROD CHECK: POST /parse with a phrase the LITERAL match misses, e.g.
#     "just book a hotel in Lisbon", and assert hotel-only scope is detected.
#     Control: "just a hotel in Lisbon", which the old literal match catches.
#     Both must pass after; only the control passes before. That contrast IS
